{
  "date": "2026-09-30",
  "status": "passed (awaiting user confirmation)",
  "baseline_commit": "3c9c32f",
  "scope": "Stage 5b (D29): magnon thermal Hall conductivity kappa_xy^2D / T per layer in units of k_B^2 / hbar, on the common pipeline.",
  "decisions": {
    "D29 (5b details, 2026-09-30)": "kappa is evaluated in pair form so that it is defined for degenerate and crossing bands (a degenerate group contributes c2 Tr F); per-band curvature and Chern numbers keep the 5a policy (NaN when not separated). Zero modes follow D25: candidates stop the calculation until gapless is given; with zero modes kappa is computed with a warning and its mesh convergence must be recorded."
  },
  "added": {
    "code-space/spintoolkit/observables/berry.py": "thermal_hall, ThermalHall (kappa_over_t in pair form, kappa_over_t_band_sum for comparison, zero-mode decision), c2_weight, c2_weight_derivative",
    "code-space/tests/test_methods/test_berry.py": "7 thermal Hall tests (20 in the file)",
    "examples/lswt_stage5b_check.py": "this record"
  },
  "formula": "kappa^2D / T = -(k_B^2 / hbar)(1 / A_cell) < sum_n c2(rho_n) Omega_n >_k over particle bands (Matsumoto and Murakami, PRB 84, 184406 (2011)). Pair form: particle-particle terms (c2_n - c2_m) / (E_n - E_m) * [-2 Im(A_nm B_mn)] / (E_n - E_m), with the divided difference by the midpoint derivative dc2/dE = -ln(1 + 1/rho)^2 rho (1 + rho) / t for relative separations below 1e-6, and zero for pairs within band_gap_cutoff (exact degeneracy: equal weights); particle-hole terms as in the band sum; a particle-hole pair within the cutoff (zero mode on the mesh) gives NaN. SI: kappa^2D [W/K] = kappa_over_t * k_B^2 T / hbar, T = t E0 / k_B.",
  "findings": [
    "Haldane magnons: the implementation equals an independent two-band calculation (curvature from finite differences of d(k), c2 by quadrature) within 3.8e-11; the textbook two-band curvature Omega_-/+ = +/-(1/2) d.(d_x d x d_y d) also confirms the 5a sign pointwise.",
    "Pair form = band sum within 1e-16 whenever the bands are separated (Haldane, Kitaev, NBCP); t -> 0 is exponentially small, t -> infinity decays as 1/t (sum of Chern numbers zero), and the Kitaev [111] value reverses exactly under field reversal.",
    "Coplanar Heisenberg states give kappa = 0 (Neel, 120 degrees, canted triangular: <= 5e-17); for Neel and 120 degrees the band sum is undefined (NaN) because the bands are degenerate or touch, so the pair form is what makes this null test possible.",
    "Continuity: Haldane kappa / T at t = 0.3 goes to zero linearly as D -> 0 (-0.99 D, -0.95 D at D = 1e-3, 1e-2; 7e-18 at D = 0) while the Chern numbers jump from +-1 to undefined.",
    "The existing SI routine observables.topology.Topology on the same k data equals the converted value within 8e-15 (NBCP Y, 0.2, 0.5, 1 K).",
    "Correction of the 5b plan: the pair form does not improve mesh convergence. For separated bands it is algebraically the band sum; the large opposite curvatures of nearly degenerate bands cancel at each k in both forms. Its gain is being defined for degenerate and crossing bands.",
    "NBCP (J_PD or J_Gamma = 0.01 meV, gapless by D25): the curvature is concentrated near small avoided crossings (particle band gaps 2e-4 to 1e-2 meV, |Omega| up to 8e3), and uniform meshes converge slowly or erratically. N = 96 -> 192: Y J_PD and V J_PD change by 2-10 percent; V J_Gamma by about 7 percent after an outlier at N = 48; Y J_Gamma nearly doubles at N = 192 where the mesh meets a near crossing (gap 2e-4 meV). NBCP values need a convergence check beyond uniform meshes (adaptive refinement near small gaps) before physical use."
  ],
